Jordan M.: Repro I saw last week: our JS fetch helper was doing `JSON.stringify(payload)` but payload.input had already been stringified by upstream code, so the server received `"["hello"]"`. The embedding pipeline then saw a JSON string and tried to treat it as a single-item token vector. Quick repro script: ```node repro.js
const body = { model: 'text-embedding-1536', input: JSON.stringify(['hello']) }
// fetch(..., { body: JSON.stringify(body) }) // causes double-wrap```
